From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:44:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] vello_cpu: a clip layer nothing is drawn in is not pushed

`push_clip_layer` now keeps the layer back and gives it to the dispatcher
just before the first draw inside it; a clip layer popped before any draw
is dropped. Such a layer changes no pixel, and pushing it costs the clip
path's strips and the layer's bookkeeping. A draw of an empty path (a
space's glyph) does not count as a draw, nor does one whose paint covers
no area. A held layer also goes to the dispatcher before any other layer,
and before a clip path or clip rectangle is pushed or popped, so its clip
is cut by the same clips as before.

The clip_overflow test now draws in its clip layer, which it needs for
the layer to be pushed at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
